{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"fe7e5276-e8ff-43fc-8db1-4caf7f0161c2\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A denominational public Hindu temple claims Article 26(b) to exclude an entire class of Hindus from worship. What did the Sri Venkataramana Devaru discussion support?\",\"hi\":\"एक सांप्रदायिक सार्वजनिक हिंदू मंदिर हिंदुओं के पूरे वर्ग को उपासना से बाहर रखने के लिए अनुच्छेद 26(b) का दावा करता है। श्री वेंकटरमण देवारू की विवेचना क्या समर्थन करती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 26(b) always defeats Article 25(2)(b)\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 26(b) हमेशा अनुच्छेद 25(2)(b) पर प्रभावी होता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 26(b) is read subject to Article 25(2)(b) for temple entry, giving effect to both provisions harmoniously\",\"hi\":\"मंदिर-प्रवेश के लिए अनुच्छेद 26(b) को अनुच्छेद 25(2)(b) के अधीन पढ़ा जाता है, ताकि दोनों उपबंधों को सामंजस्यपूर्ण प्रभाव मिले\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 27 governs temple entry\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 27 मंदिर-प्रवेश नियंत्रित करता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 28(1) abolishes denominations\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 28(1) संप्रदायों को समाप्त करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=81 — Judgment, paragraphs 112-113, PDF page 81: individual and denominational rights; Article 26(b) read subject to Article 25(2)(b); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Aishat Shifa v. State of Karnataka, 2022 Supreme Court split decision (discussion of Sri Venkataramana Devaru)\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=81\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraphs 112-113, PDF page 81: individual and denominational rights; Article 26(b) read subject to Article 25(2)(b)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Aishat Shifa judgment discussing Sri Venkataramana Devaru, paragraphs 112-113, official Supreme Court PDF page 81; Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45; Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fcffd203-e4b0-4610-b548-61b9ed896dcd\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to NCERT, cultural-minority protection extends beyond religion to which identities?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT के अनुसार सांस्कृतिक अल्पसंख्यक-सुरक्षा धर्म से आगे किन पहचानों तक जाती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only occupational groups\",\"hi\":\"केवल व्यावसायिक समूह\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Linguistic and cultural minorities\",\"hi\":\"भाषायी और सांस्कृतिक अल्पसंख्यक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only political parties\",\"hi\":\"केवल राजनीतिक दल\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only taxpayers\",\"hi\":\"केवल करदाता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 29 and 30(1), PDF page 46 (document page 15); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=15 — Printed page 40, PDF page 15: linguistic/cultural minorities, conservation, institutions and non-discrimination in aid\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 29 and 30(1), PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=15\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 40, PDF page 15: linguistic/cultural minorities, conservation, institutions and non-discrimination in aid\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 40; Constitution of India, Articles 29 and 30(1), official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fc333e98-e678-4af9-803f-a6b6e57ba60f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A State-aided college compels every adult student to attend a religious ceremony despite written refusal. Which conclusion is strongest?\",\"hi\":\"एक राज्य-सहायता प्राप्त महाविद्यालय लिखित असहमति के बावजूद प्रत्येक वयस्क विद्यार्थी को धार्मिक समारोह में उपस्थित होने के लिए बाध्य करता है। सबसे मजबूत निष्कर्ष कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The compulsion is valid because aid removes all consent rights\",\"hi\":\"विवशता वैध है क्योंकि सहायता सभी सहमति-अधिकार समाप्त कर देती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only Article 27 can apply\",\"hi\":\"केवल अनुच्छेद 27 लागू हो सकता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The compulsion conflicts with Article 28(3)\",\"hi\":\"विवशता अनुच्छेद 28(3) से असंगत है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The student must first be a minor\",\"hi\":\"विद्यार्थी का पहले अवयस्क होना आवश्यक है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fbdd00ba-9bc4-49af-96b8-a31adf1de771\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How must property protected by Article 26(d) be administered?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 26(d) से संरक्षित संपत्ति का प्रशासन कैसे किया जाना चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"In accordance with law\",\"hi\":\"विधि के अनुसार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Without any legal regulation\",\"hi\":\"किसी विधिक विनियमन के बिना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only by Parliament\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद द्वारा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only after a referendum\",\"hi\":\"केवल जनमत-संग्रह के बाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fabaf75e-0f61-4acf-866a-6add412a960f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A school is wholly State-funded, State-administered, and was established under a trust requiring religious instruction. Which combined reading of Article 28 is correct?\",\"hi\":\"एक विद्यालय पूर्णतः राज्य-पोषित और राज्य-प्रशासित है तथा ऐसे न्यास के अधीन स्थापित हुआ था जिसमें धार्मिक शिक्षा अपेक्षित है। अनुच्छेद 28 का कौन-सा संयुक्त पाठ सही है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Clause (1) applies without any exception and clause (3) is irrelevant\",\"hi\":\"खंड (1) बिना अपवाद लागू होता है और खंड (3) अप्रासंगिक है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Clause (2) permits compulsory worship for every minor\",\"hi\":\"खंड (2) प्रत्येक अवयस्क के लिए अनिवार्य उपासना की अनुमति देता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The trust automatically ends State administration\",\"hi\":\"न्यास स्वतः राज्य प्रशासन समाप्त कर देता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Clause (2) supplies the instruction exception, while clause (3) still protects consent against compelled participation in a recognised or aided institution\",\"hi\":\"खंड (2) धार्मिक शिक्षा का अपवाद देता है, जबकि खंड (3) मान्यताप्राप्त या सहायता-प्राप्त संस्था में विवश भागीदारी के विरुद्ध सहमति की रक्षा करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f78d17d6-9bb2-4b46-8957-a67fcaef9256\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Students respectfully stand during the National Anthem but decline to sing because of a sincere religious belief. Which precedent was cited as upholding their protection?\",\"hi\":\"विद्यार्थी राष्ट्रगान के समय सम्मानपूर्वक खड़े रहते हैं, पर सच्चे धार्मिक विश्वास के कारण गाने से इनकार करते हैं। उनकी सुरक्षा को मान्यता देने वाले किस पूर्वनिर्णय का उल्लेख किया गया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Rev. Stainislaus\",\"hi\":\"रेव. स्टेनिस्लॉस\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Bijoe Emmanuel v. State of Kerala\",\"hi\":\"बिजो इमैनुएल बनाम केरल राज्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Sri Venkataramana Devaru\",\"hi\":\"श्री वेंकटरमण देवारू\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A tax-appropriation case under Article 27\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 27 का कर-विनियोग वाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=86 — Judgment, paragraph 116, PDF page 86: students stood respectfully but did not sing the National Anthem; Article 25 protection discussed; Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Aishat Shifa v. State of Karnataka, 2022 Supreme Court split decision (discussion of Bijoe Emmanuel)\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=86\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraph 116, PDF page 86: students stood respectfully but did not sing the National Anthem; Article 25 protection discussed\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Aishat Shifa judgment discussing Bijoe Emmanuel, paragraph 116, official Supreme Court PDF page 86; Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f671fb6a-6bac-401e-803b-bf60fc717e55\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does section 7 do to a bonded labourer’s property encumbered in connection with bonded debt?\",\"hi\":\"बंधित ऋण से संबंधित भार वाली बंधित श्रमिक की संपत्ति के लिए धारा 7 क्या करती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Frees it from the related mortgage, charge, lien or other encumbrance\",\"hi\":\"उसे संबंधित बंधक, भार, धारणाधिकार या अन्य विल्लंगम से मुक्त करती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Transfers it permanently to the creditor\",\"hi\":\"उसे स्थायी रूप से लेनदार को देती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Requires its destruction\",\"hi\":\"उसका विनाश अपेक्षित करती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Converts it into public property\",\"hi\":\"उसे सार्वजनिक संपत्ति बनाती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=5 — Sections 7-12, PDF page 5: property, homestead and District Magistrate duties\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976 (Act 19 of 1976)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=5\",\"citation\":\"Sections 7-12, PDF page 5: property, homestead and District Magistrate duties\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976, sections 7-12, official India Code PDF page 5\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f63d9e04-16a4-4446-8a7a-b6baea8e2f0f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which clause of Article 26 protects establishing and maintaining religious and charitable institutions?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 26 का कौन-सा खंड धार्मिक और पूर्त संस्थाओं की स्थापना और पोषण की रक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Clause (d)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (d)\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Clause (a)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (a)\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Clause (c)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (c)\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Clause (b)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (b)\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5237f06-d1be-47a5-b485-36c365286681\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the immediate effect of section 4(1) of the Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act?\",\"hi\":\"बंधित श्रम पद्धति (उत्सादन) अधिनियम की धारा 4(1) का तात्कालिक प्रभाव क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It creates a new bonded debt\",\"hi\":\"यह नया बंधित ऋण बनाती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It abolishes the system and frees bonded labourers from the obligation to render bonded labour\",\"hi\":\"यह पद्धति समाप्त कर बंधित श्रमिकों को बंधित श्रम देने के दायित्व से मुक्त करती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It permits forced labour by contract\",\"hi\":\"यह संविदा से बलात् श्रम अनुमति देती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It applies only to future courts\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल भावी न्यायालयों पर लागू होती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=3 — Sections 2-4, PDF page 3: definitions, overriding effect and abolition of bonded labour system\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976 (Act 19 of 1976)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=3\",\"citation\":\"Sections 2-4, PDF page 3: definitions, overriding effect and abolition of bonded labour system\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976, sections 2-4, official India Code PDF page 3\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f05a9e5e-72bd-4e7c-a424-198550767fa8\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"When a private contractor violates Article 23, what constitutional responsibility did the PUDR discussion place on the State?\",\"hi\":\"जब निजी ठेकेदार अनुच्छेद 23 का उल्लंघन करे, PUDR की विवेचना ने राज्य पर कौन-सी संवैधानिक जिम्मेदारी रखी?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"To ignore every private violation\",\"hi\":\"हर निजी उल्लंघन की उपेक्षा करना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"To take necessary steps to stop the violation and ensure observance of the right\",\"hi\":\"उल्लंघन रोकने और अधिकार का पालन सुनिश्चित करने हेतु आवश्यक कदम उठाना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"To convert the contractor into a court\",\"hi\":\"ठेकेदार को न्यायालय में बदलना\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"To suspend Article 23\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 23 निलंबित करना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\"